    "whyImportant": "Mastering Two-Phase Locking (2PL) is critical because modern enterprise workloads demand optimal execution speeds and minimal memory overhead. Without a rigorous understanding of this topic's underlying invariants and execution boundaries, application bottlenecks can emerge silently under production stress. This concept bridges basic programming logic with hardware-level optimizations, ensuring that data manipulation pipelines operate within predictable asymptotic bounds. For system designers, selecting or implementing Two-Phase Locking (2PL) is an essential design decision that directly impacts database reads, networking efficiency, and concurrent throughput constraints.",
