  "slug": "game-phys-aabb",
  "markdown": "# Game Physics: Axis-Aligned Bounding Boxes (AABB)\n\nAn **Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB)** is a rectangular volume whose edges are aligned parallel to the coordinate axes of the world system. \n\nBecause they do not rotate, checking if two AABBs overlap is extremely fast, requiring only basic scalar comparisons. AABBs are the primary bounding volumes used in the **Broad Phase** of collision pipelines and inside spatial partition trees (like octrees or BVHs).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Mathematical Representation\n\nAn AABB in 3D is represented in one of two ways:\n\n### 1.1 Min/Max Coordinate Form\nDefined by its minimum corner vector $\\mathbf{p}_{\\text{min}}$ and maximum corner vector $\\mathbf{p}_{\\text{max}}$:\n\n$$\\mathbf{p}_{\\text{min}} = \\begin{pmatrix} x_{\\text{min}} \\\\ y_{\\text{min}} \\\\ z_{\\text{min}} \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{p}_{\\text{max}} = \\begin{pmatrix} x_{\\text{max}} \\\\ y_{\\text{max}} \\\\ z_{\\text{max}} \\end{pmatrix}$$\n\nThis is the most common form for quick overlap checks.\n\n### 1.2 Center/Extent Form\nDefined by its center position vector $\\mathbf{c}$ and half-widths vector $\\mathbf{e}$:\n\n$$\\mathbf{p}_{\\text{min}} = \\mathbf{c} - \\mathbf{e}, \\quad \\mathbf{p}_{\\text{max}} = \\mathbf{c} + \\mathbf{e}$$\n\n---\n\n## 2. AABB vs. AABB Overlap Check\n\nTwo 3D AABBs (A and B) overlap if and only if their projections overlap on all three coordinate axes simultaneously:\n\n$$\\text{Overlap}_x = A_{\\text{min},x} \\le B_{\\text{max},x} \\land A_{\\text{max},x} \\ge B_{\\text{min},x}$$\n$$\\text{Overlap}_y = A_{\\text{min},y} \\le B_{\\text{max},y} \\land A_{\\text{max},y} \\ge B_{\\text{min},y}$$\n$$\\text{Overlap}_z = A_{\\text{min},z} \\le B_{\\text{max},z} \\land A_{\\text{max},z} \\ge B_{\\text{min},z}$$\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- AABB A -->\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"40\" width=\"120\" height=\"90\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"130\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" />\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"145\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Amin (xmin, ymin)</text>\n  \n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"40\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" />\n  <text x=\"180\" y=\"30\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Amax</text>\n  \n  <!-- AABB B (Overlapping) -->\n  <rect x=\"170\" y=\"100\" width=\"120\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"180\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" />\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"195\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Bmin</text>\n  \n  <circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"100\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" />\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Bmax</text>\n  \n  <!-- Intersecting Area -->\n  <rect x=\"170\" y=\"100\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#ef4444\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1\" />\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11\">Overlap Zone</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\nIf any of these conditions are `false`, the boxes are separated, and no collision occurs.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dynamic Updates (Rotating Entities)\n\nWhen an entity rotates, its AABB must expand to contain it, as the bounding box itself cannot rotate.\n\nTo construct the new AABB from a rotated OBB (with rotation matrix $R$ and extents $\\mathbf{e}_{\\text{local}}$):\n\n$$e_{\\text{world},i} = \\sum_{j=1}^{3} |R_{i,j}| e_{\\text{local},j}$$\n\nThis calculation expands the AABB, ensuring the rotated object remains completely enveloped.\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Expanded AABB -->\n  <rect x=\"160\" y=\"30\" width=\"180\" height=\"160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"170\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\">Expanded AABB</text>\n  \n  <!-- Rotated Object (OBB) -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(250,110) rotate(35)\">\n    <rect x=\"-80\" y=\"-30\" width=\"160\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"4\" />\n    <text x=\"-40\" y=\"5\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\">Rotated OBB</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Example (Python)\n\n```python\nclass AABB:\n    def __init__(self, min_pt, max_pt):\n        self.min = list(min_pt) # (x, y, z)\n        self.max = list(max_pt) # (x, y, z)\n        \n    def intersects(self, other):\n        # Overlap check along X axis\n        if self.min[0] > other.max[0] or self.max[0] < other.min[0]:\n            return False\n            \n        # Overlap check along Y axis\n        if self.min[1] > other.max[1] or self.max[1] < other.min[1]:\n            return False\n            \n        # Overlap check along Z axis\n        if self.min[2] > other.max[2] or self.max[2] < other.min[2]:\n            return False\n            \n        # Overlap exists on all axes -> Intersection detected\n        return True\n\n# Test: box A from (0,0,0) to (2,2,2) and box B from (1.5,1.5,1.5) to (3,3,3)\naabb_a = AABB((0.0, 0.0, 0.0), (2.0, 2.0, 2.0))\naabb_b = AABB((1.5, 1.5, 1.5), (3.0, 3.0, 3.0))\nprint(\"Overlap detected:\", aabb_a.intersects(aabb_b)) # Expected: True\n```\n",
  "title": "Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB)",
  "tagline": "Min/Max coordinates, constant-time overlap checks, and dynamic box expansion.",
  "category": "Game Developer",
