  "slug": "game-phys-sweep",
  "markdown": "# Game Physics: Sort & Sweep (Sweep & Prune)\n\n**Sort & Sweep** (commonly called **Sweep & Prune**) is a highly optimized algorithm used in the **Broad Phase** of collision detection. It reduces the number of candidate bounding box overlap checks by projecting 3D boxes onto coordinate axes and sorting their intervals.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Temporal Coherence & Insertion Sort\n\nIn games, objects move small distances between consecutive frames. This characteristic is called **Temporal Coherence**. \n\nIf we sort the positions of all objects along an axis, their sorted order will change very little from one frame to the next:\n\n```\nFrame n:   [Object A] [Object B] [Object C]\nFrame n+1: [Object A] [Object C] [Object B]  (Only B and C swapped!)\n```\n\nTo exploit this, Sweep & Prune uses **Insertion Sort** to sort the boundary coordinates.\n*   While Insertion Sort has a worst-case complexity of $O(N^2)$ for unsorted data, it runs in **$O(N)$ time** on nearly-sorted lists.\n*   This makes it the fastest sorting algorithm for tracking frame-to-frame movements in games.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Endpoint Array and Active List\n\nTo implement Sweep & Prune along a coordinate axis (e.g. the X-axis):\n\n1.  **Endpoint Array:** For every object, we create two endpoints: a **Min Endpoint** ($x_{\\text{min}}$) and a **Max Endpoint** ($x_{\\text{max}}$). We store all endpoints in a single flat array.\n2.  **Sorting:** Run an insertion sort on this array at the start of the physics update.\n3.  **Active List Sweep:** Traverse the sorted array from left to right:\n    *   When you hit a **Min Endpoint**, add the object to the **Active List** and generate a collision candidate pair with every other object currently in the Active List.\n    *   When you hit a **Max Endpoint**, remove the object from the Active List.\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Axis line -->\n  <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"460\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-blue)\" />\n  \n  <!-- Endpoints timeline -->\n  <!-- A_min (60) -->\n  <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"160\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" />\n  <text x=\"65\" y=\"180\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">A_min</text>\n  \n  <!-- B_min (120) -->\n  <circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"160\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" />\n  <text x=\"145\" y=\"180\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">B_min</text>\n\n  <!-- A_max (200) -->\n  <circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"160\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" />\n  <text x=\"225\" y=\"180\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">A_max</text>\n\n  <!-- B_max (280) -->\n  <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"160\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" />\n  <text x=\"305\" y=\"180\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">B_max</text>\n\n  <!-- C_min (360) -->\n  <circle cx=\"390\" cy=\"160\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#a855f7\" />\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"180\" fill=\"#a855f7\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">C_min</text>\n  \n  <!-- active list trace blocks -->\n  <!-- at index 0 (60) -->\n  <rect x=\"70\" y=\"30\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" />\n  <text x=\"75\" y=\"44\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Active: [A]</text>\n  \n  <!-- at index 1 (120) -->\n  <rect x=\"130\" y=\"55\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" />\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"69\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Active: [A, B]</text>\n  <!-- Overlap detected! (A, B) -->\n  <path d=\"M 160 85 L 160 145\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 2\" />\n  <text x=\"170\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\">Overlap Pair (A, B)</text>\n\n  <!-- at index 2 (240) -->\n  <rect x=\"225\" y=\"30\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" />\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"44\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Active: [B]</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 3. Multi-Dimensional Sweep & Prune\n\nIn a 3D game world, sorting along a single axis can generate false positives if objects overlap on one axis but are separated on the others. To solve this, engines extend the algorithm:\n\n*   **Multi-Axis Sweep & Prune:** Sorts endpoints along all three coordinate axes (X, Y, Z) independently. A candidate pair is only sent to the narrow phase if its bounding intervals overlap on **all three axes**.\n*   **Dynamic Axis Selection:** The engine runs a variance check on object coordinates and sweeps along the axis with the highest variance (where objects are most spread out), minimizing sorting density.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Example (Python)\n\n```python\nclass Endpoint:\n    def __init__(self, val, is_min, obj_id):\n        self.val = float(val)\n        self.is_min = bool(is_min)\n        self.obj_id = obj_id\n\ndef sweep_and_prune_1d(objects):\n    # objects: list of dicts {\"id\": ID, \"min\": float, \"max\": float}\n    # 1. Build endpoint list\n    endpoints = []\n    for obj in objects:\n        endpoints.append(Endpoint(obj[\"min\"], True, obj[\"id\"]))\n        endpoints.append(Endpoint(obj[\"max\"], False, obj[\"id\"]))\n        \n    # 2. Sort endpoints (simulate insertion sort on nearly-sorted data)\n    endpoints.sort(key=lambda ep: ep.val)\n    \n    # 3. Sweep active list\n    active_list = set()\n    candidate_pairs = []\n    \n    for ep in endpoints:\n        if ep.is_min:\n            # Generate candidate pairs with all current active objects\n            for active_id in active_list:\n                pair = tuple(sorted((ep.obj_id, active_id)))\n                candidate_pairs.append(pair)\n            active_list.add(ep.obj_id)\n        else:\n            active_list.remove(ep.obj_id)\n            \n    return candidate_pairs\n\n# Test case\nobjs = [\n    {\"id\": \"A\", \"min\": 1.0, \"max\": 4.0},\n    {\"id\": \"B\", \"min\": 2.0, \"max\": 5.0},\n    {\"id\": \"C\", \"min\": 6.0, \"max\": 8.0}\n]\nprint(\"Collision Candidates:\", sweep_and_prune_1d(objs)) # Expected: [('A', 'B')]\n```\n",
  "title": "Sort & Sweep (Sweep & Prune)",
  "tagline": "Temporal coherence, endpoint arrays, insertion sort, and active list sweeps.",
